    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with an aggressive outfield-heavy attack, anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (75.66) and **Mickey Moniak** (72.51). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary asset; beyond his elite projected output, he benefits from a rare combination of facing a favorable pitcher in Trevor McDonald and a high-probability stolen base environment against a pitcher with a slow delivery. While **James Wood** (68.23) projects exceptionally well due to his elite 0.416 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot, he carries a 30% rain risk warning that could shorten his day. We are capitalizing on park factors for **Mickey Moniak**, whose score is boosted significantly by a 14% park adjustment and a strong platoon advantage, making him a high-upside play against Max Meyer.\n\nWe are hunting for value in the middle infield and corner spots, relying on **Brice Turang** (65.83) to provide stable production against Andrew Abbott. Although **Austin Riley** (61.66) and **Seiya Suzuki** (61.43) sit just above the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, both are locked in due to favorable park factors and, in **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s case, beneficial wind conditions. The toughest bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, whose 44.93 score kept him firmly in the conversation. However, the optimizer sidelined **Kyle Karros** in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**; while their scores are lower, the positional scarcity and the favorable park conditions associated with their respective matchups against J.T. Ginn provided a more strategic path to meeting our daily Roto targets. We will continue to monitor the status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, and the rest of the lineup, as all assignments are based on assumed batting orders pending official confirmation.",
